239
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:39,500
I heard one scholar say Jesus spent three years interacting with the Pharisees and they

240
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:43,220
only tried to kill him once or twice and it was based on the Old Testament law.

241
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:46,740
He spent one week with the Sadducees and he's dead.

242
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,380
These are bad people with bad intentions.

243
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:53,120
And both groups are pretty angry with Jesus.

244
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:58,600
He tells them three pointed parables aimed directly at them for this specific cultural moment.

245
00:15:58,600 --> 00:15:59,740
This is important context.

246
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:04,600
This is not a spiritual analogy about how God interacts with all of his people at all times.

247
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:09,480
This is a direct warning to this group of people for this specific time.

248
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:15,760
So with that in mind, what we aren't going to do is we aren't going to read this parable

249
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:20,760
as a spiritual allegory written to us about people go, about how people go to heaven or

250
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:21,380
hell when they die.

251
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:24,400
Right?

252
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:28,460
Does that make any of us feel a little bit better after what we just read?

253
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:30,520
Makes me feel a lot better.

254
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,080
All right.

255
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:37,880
Instead, we are going to read it to see what it says about what God is like, what his kingdom

256
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:44,340
is like, and how God invites people to participate in his kingdom, and the type of people who

257
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:48,660
will end up being excluded from his kingdom if they do not heed his warnings and repent.

258
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:51,620
That's what we're going to do with the rest of our time this morning.

259
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:52,060
Sound good?

260
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:53,280
Okay.

261
00:16:53,280 --> 00:17:01,900
My first point is that God's kingdom is like a joyous celebration, not a list of commands.

262
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,440
This is the first reminder.

263
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:09,180
This is the first kind of backdrop of what Jesus is saying the kingdom is like.

264
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:14,680
The kingdom of heaven is like a king who prepared a wedding banquet for his son.

265
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:20,180
He sent servants to those who had been invited to the banquet and told them to come.

266
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:22,200
We cannot miss the backdrop of the story.

267
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:27,780
Jesus says that the kingdom of God, the rule and reign of God breaking into the world is like

268
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:33,920
a lavish, joyous party thrown by the creator of all things to honor his son.

269
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,580
This is what God's kingdom is like.

270
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:39,340
It's a joyous celebration.

271
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:46,440
And it's meant for people who are filled with joy over the idea of honoring Jesus.

272
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:50,960
We've been invited into a personal relationship with the son.

273
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:54,620
He so values you.

274
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:59,960
That you get a special invitation to his party.

275
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:04,880
And you're meant to come out of joy, not obligation or duty or fear.

276
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:15,540
God's kingdom is a joyous celebration that you are invited to participate in joyfully and willingly.

277
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:21,560
And Jesus models this throughout his life and ministry.

278
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:27,860
How much of the Gospels when we read them is Jesus throwing a party, right?

279
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:32,900
Or taking charge at somebody else's table and making it a joyous occasion,

280
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:36,220
a celebration of what God is doing and wants to do through his kingdom.

281
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:43,220
He so much loves to party that the religious leaders say that he is a drunkard and a glutton.

282
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:46,540
Like this is what Jesus is known for.

283
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:51,000
He's known for celebrating the goodness of God all around him.

284
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:57,180
For celebrating people who have come to know, to taste and see that the Lord is good.

285
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:02,920
When somebody who is a sinner repents and comes to know and taste and see that the Lord is good,

286
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,380
Jesus says, let's throw a party and let's celebrate.

287
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:10,560
It's like the father from the parable of the prodigal son.

288
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,620
It's time to celebrate.

289
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:15,480
This son of mine was dead and now he's alive.

290
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,180
This is what God's kingdom is like.

291
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:19,540
It's like dead people coming to life again.

292
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:23,240
It's something worthy of celebration.

293
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:38,120
It's an epic party being thrown for anyone who is able to truly see that surrender to God isn't calculated sacrificial transaction we make so that we get to heaven when we die.

294
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:44,580
It's an eternal and life transforming relationship that leads to abundant joy no matter our circumstance.

295
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:50,200
And I don't know how much time you guys have spent around Christians lately.

296
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:55,820
We're not always the most joyful bunch.

297
00:19:55,820 --> 00:20:03,140
I think many of us in the kingdom have lost the plot.

298
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:08,680
We've made our faith far more transactional and intellectual than relational.

299
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:15,960
And I think we need a healthy reminder that surrender to Jesus is not a spiritual workout to get through.

300
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:20,900
But a celebration to joyfully participate in.

301
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,200
This is God's kingdom.

302
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:29,620
It's an invitation to celebrate who he is and what he has done for you and for me.

303
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:34,520
It's a celebration of death to life.

304
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,840
Slavery to freedom.

305
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,720
Religion.

306
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,180
To joy.

307
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:44,000
That's the backdrop.

308
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,280
Pretty good stuff so far, right?

309
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:48,320
But as you know, it's going to get worse here in a second.

310
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:55,760
So now the king moves from his original save the date invitation.

311
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:59,480
He'd sent this invitation out to a group of people and they said they were going to come.

312
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,760
Right?

313
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:01,840
It was the save the date.

314
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:05,480
It was the basic general like, hey, I'm throwing a banquet to celebrate my son.

315
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,620
And this group of people are like, yeah, we're in.

316
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:08,260
Count us in.

317
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:09,880
Of course we want to come to a celebration.

318
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:10,880
Of the king.

319
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,380
That makes us feel important.

320
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,240
And it means we're probably going to get good food and good drink.

321
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:15,480
Right?

322
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:19,000
So the king moves from the save the date to the real invitation.

323
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,960
He says, now it is time to celebrate.

324
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,140
The food is ready.

325
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:24,200
The drink is ready.

326
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,800
Come and celebrate.

327
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:28,800
And there is an entire group of people who are originally RSVP'd.

328
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:30,400
Yes, we're in.

329
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:34,740
Who for a number of reasons are no longer interested in coming.

330
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:44,200
It says those who had been invited to the banquet tell them to come, but they refused to come.

331
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,880
They accepted this general invitation.

332
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:51,600
But as the party begins to take shape, it doesn't look the way they thought it would.

333
00:21:54,820 --> 00:22:02,380
The kingdom of God is taking shape before the very eyes of the Jewish leaders, before the eyes of the Sadducees and the Pharisees.

334
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:13,520
These are the people who were entrusted, who were invited to participate in God's kingdom until he comes to make a way for people to come and worship and to obey God's law.

335
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:18,500
And they said, yes, but when God himself shows up, they're like, oh, no, we didn't think it was going to look like this.

336
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:22,680
This is not what we signed up for.

337
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,640
This is not what we RSVP'd to.

338
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:37,780
How many people attending churches like ours all over this country are interested in the idea of being an honored guest in God's kingdom?

339
00:22:37,780 --> 00:22:48,580
So far as the kingdom looks the way they want it to with the guest list that they want, as long as it's not inconvenient to more pressing matters in their lives.

340
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:54,100
Corey wants me to preach.

341
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:55,060
Does anybody else want me to preach?

342
00:22:55,060 --> 00:23:11,400
How many people attend churches like ours on a weekly basis who love the idea of being a part of God's kingdom, as long as they get to define what it looks like and who's invited?

343
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:20,160
The religious leaders of this time and many of us still to this day, we love the idea of attending a wedding feast with the king.

344
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:24,880
But when the king's son wants to throw a party, unlike the party we imagined, we opt out.

345
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:33,500
Because for many of us, our faith is more about what it does for us than what it does to honor the son.

346
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:38,500
The kingdom is like a wedding celebration.

347
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:43,460
And just like attending a wedding, you don't do it for what you can get out of it.

348
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:46,260
You do it to honor the bride and the groom.

349
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:48,540
So is the kingdom of God.

350
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:52,180
We don't attend, we don't show up to the kingdom for what we get out of it.

351
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,880
We show up to the kingdom to honor the son.

352
00:23:54,880 --> 00:24:04,240
Verse four.

353
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:12,900
Then he sent more servants and said, tell those who have been invited, I have prepared my dinner.

354
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:16,500
My oxen and fattened cattle have been butchered and everything is ready.

355
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:18,900
Come to the wedding banquet.

356
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:25,400
Second thing I want to emphasize here is that God's invitation to his kingdom is patient and persistent.

357
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:34,860
I don't think we need a ton of cultural or historical background on first century kings to realize that this is a crazy generous move on part of the king.

358
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:38,820
You guys read about first century kings?

359
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:44,000
Do they typically give second chances to people who outright disrespect them?

360
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:52,240
Rejecting the king's invitation that you previously agreed to would have been unthinkable, unimaginable.

361
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:59,160
And most kings would have received it at the least as a sign of incredible disrespect and potentially treason.

362
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:02,540
Because marriages were very political, right?

363
00:25:02,540 --> 00:25:09,580
And you not showing up to the king's son getting married is you saying, I'm not interested in the direction this king is taking our land.

364
00:25:09,580 --> 00:25:21,740
And instead of laying down the hammer like most kings would have, this king sends out another set of servants to plead with the invitees, to persuade them you're missing out.

365
00:25:21,740 --> 00:25:27,300
He says, I know you.

366
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:28,100
I'm your king.

367
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,780
You don't have food like I have food.

368
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:33,260
You don't have wine like I have wine.

369
00:25:33,260 --> 00:25:38,920
You are missing out on what I am doing.

370
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:46,220
This gives me real vibes from the prodigal son, right?

371
00:25:46,220 --> 00:25:49,920
This king is like the father who's going out to the older brother.

372
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:52,660
And he's begging him, like, please come in.

373
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:54,340
You don't understand what we're doing in there.

374
00:25:54,340 --> 00:25:56,820
Your brother was dead and he's alive again.

375
00:25:56,820 --> 00:25:58,920
You don't understand what we're doing in here.

376
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:07,820
I know you're saying no because you think you know what's going on, but you don't know what's going on.

377
00:26:09,420 --> 00:26:13,300
God is patient and persistent with us even when we reject him.

378
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:23,840
Even when we harden our hearts toward his idea of a party, even when we try and redefine it in our own image, he continues to regularly invite us back to what he's doing.

379
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:38,220
The Sadducees, who I believe this part of the parable is directly confronting, they are the culmination of a long history of God's leaders rebelling against God's purposes.

380
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:45,780
Throughout the history of Israel, God is continually patient and persistent with them, pleading with them to come to the party.

381
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:58,220
Hundreds of years, hundreds of years, thousands of years, thousands of years, God has been going to his people, the leaders of his people, and asking them to come back to his purposes, to do the thing that he partnered with them to do.

382
00:26:58,220 --> 00:27:09,420
Hebrews 1 says many times, many times, and in many ways, God spoke through the prophets, and now he is speaking through his son.

383
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:20,080
This parable sounds harsh, but it's Christ's last-bitch effort, pleading with the Jewish leaders to see the beauty of God's kingdom, to repent, and to surrender to it.

384
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:30,600
This is the culmination of thousands of years of God sending prophets to his people, saying, please, come to the party, you're missing out.

385
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:37,580
And God's people continually harding their hearts to God's good purposes and saying, no, we've got it.

386
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:45,160
We've got you figured out, we've got you, we've got a system in place that allows us to be blessed and others outside to be cursed.

387
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:50,560
And God says, the whole thing was about blessing the whole world, and you're missing it, please come back.

388
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:57,020
And they kept saying no, and they killed the prophets, and they killed John the Baptist, and now he sends Jesus, and they're about to kill him.

389
00:27:57,020 --> 00:28:01,700
And Jesus says, I've been patient, I've been persistent.

390
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:06,200
I sat outside the gates of Jerusalem weeping over you.

391
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:16,540
It's time to either repent or go ahead and kill me, because everybody in this room is about to know that I'm talking about you.

392
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:34,880
So, if you're here, and you've been in an up and down wrestling match with God, I want you to know that this is the culmination of thousands of years of warning and patient persistence.

393
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:36,980
This is not God's heart towards you.

394
00:28:36,980 --> 00:28:43,720
God's heart towards you isn't condemnation, but patient and persistent invitation.

395
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:50,140
Your rebellion is hurting you, and it's hurting others, and he wants you to turn to him and experience true life.

396
00:28:50,140 --> 00:29:01,480
But unfortunately, there comes a point when some of us, we harden our hearts so much that we can't even hear it anymore.

397
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:05,720
And that's what ends up happening in this parable.

398
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:10,280
My third point is that the rejection of God's kingdom has consequences.

399
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:13,840
They paid no attention.

400
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:15,980
They went off to one to the field, one to the business.

401
00:29:15,980 --> 00:29:21,700
The rest seized his servants, mistreated them, and killed them.

402
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:22,800
The king was enraged.

403
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:26,500
He sent his army and destroyed those murderers and burned their city.

404
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:32,860
I'm not going to sit here and pretend like this is an easy passage to wrestle with.

405
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:47,420
But I think when we step back and we realize who is inviting us, what we are being invited to, and how patient God has been with us, I think we can begin to wrap our minds a little bit around this story.

406
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:53,860
Now, let's not make it too personal too soon, okay?

407
00:29:53,860 --> 00:29:56,400
Let's talk about the Sadducees before I talk about you and me.

408
00:29:56,400 --> 00:30:01,060
Let's make it impersonal before we get personal.

409
00:30:01,060 --> 00:30:03,640
The Sadducees are just downright bad people.

410
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:05,880
Very bad people.

411
00:30:06,420 --> 00:30:12,020
They were appointed by God to lead the nation of Israel in worshiping him and obedience to his law.

412
00:30:12,020 --> 00:30:15,960
Worship and obedience, again, that was intended to be a blessing to the whole world.

413
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:25,680
And instead, the Sadducees struck a political partnership with Rome that allowed a very small group of people to exploit their own people for their own personal gain.

414
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:28,220
They were mocking God.

415
00:30:28,220 --> 00:30:32,180
They were holding their feet down on the necks of the working class Jews.

416
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:35,860
This is spiritual abuse and corruption to the worst degree.

417
00:30:35,860 --> 00:30:46,720
And most of us, most of us, when we're confronted with the case of a bad person continually doing bad things with repeated warnings and grace extended to them,

418
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:49,640
most of us are pretty okay with that person receiving justice.

419
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,980
Right?

420
00:30:50,980 --> 00:30:54,480
I've watched the courtroom shows.

421
00:30:55,680 --> 00:31:00,760
I know how we feel about people who are abusive, who take care, who take advantage of vulnerable people.

422
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:06,480
And so we can look at this parable and say, yeah, Jesus, get those Sadducees.

423
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:08,860
They deserve it.

424
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:10,460
They've had lots of warnings.

425
00:31:10,460 --> 00:31:11,980
They're getting rich.

426
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:21,800
Their houses are literally mansions outside of Jerusalem while the working class Jews are barely surviving on like 80% tax rate.

427
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:23,120
Right?

428
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:25,400
These are bad people.

429
00:31:25,500 --> 00:31:26,080
Get them, Jesus.

430
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:30,940
Now, be personal.

431
00:31:30,940 --> 00:31:32,160
Okay?

432
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:35,300
My mom says, let's not.

433
00:31:35,300 --> 00:31:35,760
I love that.

434
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:38,400
Skip this slide because mom says so.

435
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:38,720
All right.

436
00:31:41,580 --> 00:31:53,780
God, the maker of heaven and earth, God, the maker of heaven and earth, the giver of every resource or skill that you and I will ever have or ever have had,

437
00:31:53,780 --> 00:32:02,500
the provider of the very breath in my lungs that is keeping me alive right now is inviting me to a party to celebrate his generosity.

438
00:32:03,020 --> 00:32:12,260
In a way that harmonizes with his design, blesses others around us in a way that harmonizes with his design, blesses others around us and leads to abundant life now and eternal life in the future.

439
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:27,960
And even as we refuse that invitation on repeat, God is persistent and patient to the point of offering his one and only son as a sacrifice.

440
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:34,880
And we think judgment sounds harsh because I'm a pretty good person.

441
00:32:37,760 --> 00:32:39,100
It's bullcrap.

442
00:32:39,100 --> 00:32:43,640
It is.

443
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:53,060
This is us hardening our hearts towards a gracious God and us looking back at him and saying, you're not being gracious enough.

444
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:58,160
You haven't given us enough opportunity to receive your forgiveness.

445
00:32:58,160 --> 00:33:00,180
You don't understand what it's like down here.

446
00:33:00,180 --> 00:33:04,040
You are not, and I am not a good person.

447
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:13,640
We are in direct rebellion against the God of the universe who is patiently and persistently inviting us into relationship.

448
00:33:13,640 --> 00:33:16,140
I love how Dr. Tim Keller puts it.

449
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:43,080
This is a harsh warning to a group of people who have hardened their hearts for a very, very long time.

450
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:48,220
I can't say that enough, that this is not God speaking directly to you.

451
00:33:48,220 --> 00:33:52,880
He is speaking directly to a group of people who have hardened their hearts for a very long time.

452
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:57,600
And this is his last ditch effort to say, please repent.

453
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:59,180
Please turn away.

454
00:33:59,180 --> 00:34:04,560
This parable is not intended to be used to build a theology of eternal judgment.

455
00:34:06,560 --> 00:34:15,240
Let me say that again, because a lot of people will teach this parable like this is this, like Jesus was saying this so that we would build our theology around heaven and hell based on this parable.

456
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:17,260
That's not what this parable is intended to do.

457
00:34:17,260 --> 00:34:21,120
Many actually believe, well, I'm not going to do that.

458
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:22,040
I don't have time for that.

459
00:34:22,040 --> 00:34:22,960
We'll talk about that later.

460
00:34:24,840 --> 00:34:28,980
But the persistent witness of the Bible is that God is patient and gracious.

461
00:34:28,980 --> 00:34:35,660
But judgment is coming for those who receive the invitation, but choose to reject it.

462
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:51,280
I hear as a pastor all the time when I'm interacting with people who don't believe in Jesus, one of the biggest obstacles that they have to faith is, well, what about the person in the third world country who never hears the invitation to the kingdom?

463
00:34:53,680 --> 00:35:00,020
And what I want to say to that person is, hey, let's put them off the table for a second.

464
00:35:00,020 --> 00:35:03,360
Let's talk about you who is receiving the invitation.

465
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:07,480
Because this parable is about people who received the invitation.

466
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:11,960
And you are right here in this place receiving the invitation on repeat.

467
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:20,700
And so let's stop trying to avoid you and God so that you can kind of blame shift and make an excuse to avoid interacting with the invitation that God is making you right now.

468
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:23,760
Let's stop that, and why don't you interact with this invitation?

469
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:29,120
And if you're really so concerned, this is from Brother Corey earlier this week.

470
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:33,120
If you're really so concerned about the third person in the third world country, receive the invitation.

471
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:35,100
Get on a boat and go find them.

472
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:42,860
Let's not make this an excuse that you can kind of just put off this confrontation, put off this invitation.

473
00:35:42,860 --> 00:35:46,340
Blame God for being unjust, unrighteous, not good.

474
00:35:46,340 --> 00:35:51,560
But this is between you and him, and he is extending a patient and persistent invitation to you.

475
00:35:51,560 --> 00:35:52,940
What are you going to do about it?

476
00:35:52,940 --> 00:35:57,240
All right.

477
00:35:57,240 --> 00:35:59,640
We're doing good-ish.

478
00:35:59,640 --> 00:36:05,500
Next, the invitation was always intended to bless the outsider.

479
00:36:08,380 --> 00:36:10,740
They reject the invitation.

480
00:36:10,740 --> 00:36:12,620
They kill his servants.

481
00:36:12,620 --> 00:36:15,120
He sends more servants.

482
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:21,080
He said, the wedding banquet is ready, but those I invited do not deserve to come, so go to the street corners.

483
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:23,780
Invite to the banquet anyone you find.

484
00:36:23,780 --> 00:36:24,700
That's you and me.

485
00:36:24,700 --> 00:36:26,600
Anybody.

486
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:29,040
The bad as well as the good.

487
00:36:29,840 --> 00:36:33,480
The wedding hall was filled with guests.

488
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:41,580
Israel and their leaders were always intended to be a blessing to the outsider, a beacon of light in a dark world.

489
00:36:41,580 --> 00:36:49,360
But many of them lost the plot, even after patient and persistent invitations to repent, even after prophets were sent.

490
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:55,220
God sends Jesus to become for the world what Israel couldn't.

491
00:36:55,220 --> 00:36:57,480
He is now our great high priest.

492
00:36:57,480 --> 00:37:00,940
And all are welcome to come to the party through him.

493
00:37:00,940 --> 00:37:02,660
What a blessing.

494
00:37:02,660 --> 00:37:10,720
What a joyous occasion to be unexpectedly pulled from the street and ushered into the king's palace for a wedding feast.

495
00:37:11,860 --> 00:37:14,860
This, brothers and sisters, is why we should be full of joy.

496
00:37:14,860 --> 00:37:19,760
We are undeserving, and our king is gracious and generous.

497
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:26,640
This is the crescendo of the parable, the climax of the beauty of God's kingdom.

498
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:32,020
But Jesus was spitting fires last week, right?

499
00:37:32,020 --> 00:37:40,020
So there's one final warning that we have to wrestle with in this text, and it leads me to my main point.

500
00:37:40,120 --> 00:37:42,900
The one thing I want us to remember, if we don't remember anything else,

501
00:37:42,900 --> 00:37:50,720
God's kingdom is an epic and eternal party for those who are willing to joyfully submit to the king's invitation.

502
00:37:50,720 --> 00:38:01,340
When the king came in, he saw a wedding hall filled with guests.

503
00:38:01,340 --> 00:38:04,500
He noticed one man there not wearing wedding clothes.

504
00:38:04,500 --> 00:38:08,000
And he asked, how did you get in here without wedding clothes, friend?

505
00:38:08,780 --> 00:38:09,960
I think this is really important.

506
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:12,180
The man was speechless.

507
00:38:12,180 --> 00:38:22,000
The king told the attendants, tie his hands and his feet and throw him outside to the darkness where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.

508
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:24,720
See, I think the garment represents partial submission.

509
00:38:26,660 --> 00:38:30,740
There's a category of people that want God's kingdom on their own terms.

510
00:38:30,740 --> 00:38:37,780
The dress code at a wedding is about honoring the will of the ones being celebrated.

511
00:38:38,440 --> 00:38:44,740
And so this person shows up to the wedding with no desire to honor the will of the one being celebrated.

512
00:38:44,740 --> 00:38:50,140
It's like, I'm coming to the party, but I'm coming on my own terms with my own agenda.

513
00:38:50,140 --> 00:38:53,220
I'm here, but I'm here for me.

514
00:38:54,260 --> 00:38:57,060
I'm here the way I want to be here.

515
00:38:57,860 --> 00:39:01,300
And I think this guy was speechless because he knew.

516
00:39:01,300 --> 00:39:03,800
He knew what he was doing.

517
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:05,140
He wasn't there to honor the son.

518
00:39:05,140 --> 00:39:07,080
He was there for himself.

519
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:10,540
And he could have formulated a million excuses.

520
00:39:10,540 --> 00:39:11,500
And so could we.

521
00:39:11,500 --> 00:39:13,660
He just got ripped off the street.

522
00:39:13,660 --> 00:39:15,780
I wasn't expecting to be here.

523
00:39:15,780 --> 00:39:16,480
I'm busy.

524
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:16,960
I'm tired.

525
00:39:17,020 --> 00:39:18,060
I got a lot going on.

526
00:39:18,060 --> 00:39:26,620
I think oftentimes we're entitled and we think that showing up is enough.

527
00:39:26,620 --> 00:39:32,280
But I just want to say this morning that showing up without surrender is religious idolatry.

528
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:43,640
Showing up to God's party with our agenda, wanting to do things our way is religion and idolatry.

529
00:39:43,640 --> 00:39:46,240
It isn't submission to the king.

530
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:52,140
Showing up for your honor rather than the son's is an exercise in missing the point.

531
00:39:52,140 --> 00:39:58,880
And if you think you've got excuses now, wait till you stand before king of the universe.

532
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:02,400
Think you'll be speechless.

533
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:08,380
Because I think somewhere deep down inside, those of us that approach the kingdom like this, we know.

534
00:40:08,380 --> 00:40:10,880
We know that we're not here for the son.

535
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:12,160
We're here for us.

536
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:16,220
We're not here to push forth the son's agenda.

537
00:40:16,220 --> 00:40:17,220
We're here for our agenda.

538
00:40:17,220 --> 00:40:19,520
We're here for the free food and the free drinks.

539
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:28,980
God's kingdom is an epic and eternal party for those willing to joyfully submit to the king's invitation.

540
00:40:28,980 --> 00:40:31,580
Now, here's the beautiful thing.

541
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:37,140
I love this about this parable being set to the backdrop of a wedding feast.

542
00:40:39,680 --> 00:40:42,700
Is that a wedding that you've been invited to?

543
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:45,020
Your participation is important.

544
00:40:45,020 --> 00:40:52,820
We've all been to weddings where everybody thought they were too cool to get on the dance floor.

545
00:40:52,820 --> 00:40:54,760
Right?

546
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,200
It's a lame wedding.

547
00:40:56,200 --> 00:40:57,220
Nobody's dancing.

548
00:40:57,220 --> 00:40:58,540
Nobody's celebrating.

549
00:40:59,420 --> 00:41:00,660
What are we doing?

550
00:41:00,660 --> 00:41:14,660
We've all sat at tables where people complain about the food or the drinks or the lack of drinks or the weight.

551
00:41:14,660 --> 00:41:17,600
Anybody ever sat at one of these tables at a wedding?

552
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:22,040
I'm the only one that has jerky people that go to weddings with him?

553
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:22,320
All right.

554
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,980
That's good.

555
00:41:23,980 --> 00:41:28,900
You guys, introduce me to your friends so that I can hang out with you all.

556
00:41:31,940 --> 00:41:35,080
Weddings are a place where selfish people can lose sight of the point.

557
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:40,800
And I got a bit of passive aggressive in me.

558
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:48,600
So if I'm sitting at a table, people are complaining about the weight, the food, the drink.

559
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:52,600
I'm not going to be super self-righteous here.

560
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:54,240
I've complained about food and drinking.

561
00:41:54,240 --> 00:41:59,160
But I'm preaching this morning, so I got to pretend like I'm always on point.

562
00:42:00,160 --> 00:42:05,880
But when I am on point, when I do recognize the reason that I'm there and I hear people complaining,

563
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:07,320
I got a bit of passive aggressive in me.

564
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:09,240
So there's a technique I like to do here.

565
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:17,880
What do we do when we clink the glass?

566
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:24,820
Everybody stops and we point our eyes to the reason that we're there.

567
00:42:24,820 --> 00:42:28,020
We remind ourselves of who we're honoring.

568
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:38,200
And my prayer, my prayer this morning is that this sermon

569
00:42:38,200 --> 00:42:43,760
is a clink of the glass.

570
00:42:43,760 --> 00:42:48,980
A clear reminder of what the kingdom is and what it isn't.

571
00:42:48,980 --> 00:42:52,580
Of who it is about and who it isn't.

572
00:42:54,660 --> 00:42:58,280
And my desire for each one of us in this church

573
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:02,400
is that we would be a people who joyfully show up

574
00:43:02,400 --> 00:43:06,580
and we regularly remind ourselves of why we're here.

575
00:43:06,580 --> 00:43:10,920
We set our eyes on the sun.

576
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:12,880
We honor the sun.

577
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:24,260
Even when, even when we're confronted with the reality that the kingdom might look differently than we thought it would.

578
00:43:24,260 --> 00:43:29,720
And that we're regularly willing to repent and acknowledge that we are selfish.

579
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:32,300
It says they went out and got good and bad people.

580
00:43:33,580 --> 00:43:34,660
I love that.

581
00:43:34,660 --> 00:43:37,740
I am often the bad person.

582
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:42,160
But God is gracious and persistent and patient.

583
00:43:44,020 --> 00:43:46,220
And I feel like the Holy Spirit is just meant to.

584
00:43:46,220 --> 00:43:50,180
You're missing the point.

585
00:43:50,180 --> 00:43:53,500
You're celebrating the wrong things.

586
00:43:57,500 --> 00:44:01,560
So if you're in here and you've got a heart that's hardened towards God.

587
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:08,320
Either you don't believe he's good or you think you've got more important things to do today is your reminder.

588
00:44:08,320 --> 00:44:14,260
That he is patiently and persistently inviting you to repent and to come back.

589
00:44:14,260 --> 00:44:19,960
And that the thing that he's inviting to you is an epic party that's meant to bless the whole world.

590
00:44:19,960 --> 00:44:22,580
Don't harden your heart.

591
00:44:22,580 --> 00:44:25,420
Judgment is coming.

592
00:44:25,420 --> 00:44:27,220
I don't like to preach about that.

593
00:44:27,220 --> 00:44:28,540
I don't like to preach about that.

594
00:44:28,540 --> 00:44:32,740
Biblical witness is clear that judgment is coming.

595
00:44:32,740 --> 00:44:34,060
I don't know what that looks like.

596
00:44:34,060 --> 00:44:36,800
I'm not going to expound on that.

597
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:39,360
But judgment comes for those who refuse to come to the party.

598
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:43,280
Others of us, we think we're good because we've showed up.

599
00:44:43,280 --> 00:44:46,120
But is it possible we're fooling ourselves?

600
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:50,380
Is it possible we've showed up for our own reasons and on our own terms?

601
00:44:50,380 --> 00:44:54,960
The kingdom is a party for people.

602
00:44:56,940 --> 00:45:01,140
Who show up surrendered and ready to honor the son.

603
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:09,540
And for those of us who have tasted it and seen that the Lord is good, we can tell you that this party is pretty epic.

604
00:45:11,180 --> 00:45:11,880
It's worth giving up everything for.

605
00:45:11,880 --> 00:45:13,960
It's worth giving up everything for.

606
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:15,720
Let's pray.

607
00:45:15,720 --> 00:45:26,640
Father, we, I acknowledge that this parable is a heavy parable.

608
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:36,700
God, God, that I am often insecure of how much you love me.

609
00:45:36,700 --> 00:45:41,180
And so I read things like this and I'm all in my head.

610
00:45:41,180 --> 00:45:48,020
And I just pray your Holy Spirit would do with this parable what you want to do in each of our lives.

611
00:45:49,380 --> 00:45:56,320
God, God, many of us just need to be reminded that a loving king has invited us to an epic celebration.

612
00:45:56,320 --> 00:45:59,760
It's a joyous occasion.

613
00:45:59,760 --> 00:46:07,720
God, others of us have hardened our heart towards God and we need to be warned to repent.

614
00:46:07,720 --> 00:46:25,620
God, others of us, we might think we're in here for the right reasons, but I pray, Holy Spirit, if we are not, if we have selfish intentions, may you make us aware of that.

615
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:31,020
And God, the invitation for every group of people in this room is the same.

616
00:46:31,020 --> 00:46:36,520
There is a king who's throwing an epic party and he wants all of us to come.

617
00:46:36,520 --> 00:46:39,380
And he's made a way for all of us to come.

618
00:46:39,380 --> 00:46:44,580
But we've got to be willing to surrender to that invitation.

619
00:46:44,580 --> 00:46:47,000
God, give us hearts of surrender.

620
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:50,480
In Jesus' name I pray.

621
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:51,800
Amen.
